# Copy to .env and fill in. .env is gitignored.
ANTHROPIC_API_KEY=sk-ant-...
# Local Postgres over the default unix socket; change if yours differs.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql:///enhanced_agent
# Optional: FurHat robot IP for voice mode (orchestrator/chat.py --furhat).
# Unset or unreachable falls back to plain CLI text automatically.
# FURHAT_IP=192.168.1.50
# Every routing, scope-gate, and agent LLM call walks an ordered provider
# chain: Amazon Bedrock first (if configured below), then this direct
# Anthropic API key, then OpenAI (if configured). Bedrock goes first because
# it's the provider actually reachable when this Anthropic key is degraded
# (exhausted credits, outage, rate limit), while still serving the same
# Claude models. A provider erroring on its own turn falls through to the
# next configured one; ANTHROPIC_API_KEY above is required regardless, since
# it's this chain's non-optional middle step.
#
# Optional: OpenAI fallback (last in the chain). Does NOT cover the
# self-extension code-generation step (agent_maker/generator.py runs the
# Claude Agent SDK directly, a separate mechanism this doesn't reach — that
# one only ever uses Bedrock or direct Anthropic, since the harness only
# talks to Claude models).
# OPENAI_API_KEY=sk-...
#
# Optional: Amazon Bedrock — first in the orchestrator/llm.py chain above,
# and also the preferred-first provider for self-extension code generation
# (agent_maker/maker.py, falling back to the direct Anthropic API above if
# Bedrock's own call fails). Needs both an AWS credential pair and a model
# id available in your account/region.
# AWS_ACCESS_KEY_ID=AKIA...
# AWS_SECRET_ACCESS_KEY=...
# BEDROCK_MODEL_ID=us.anthropic.claude-sonnet-4-6
# Optional: defaults to us-east-1 if unset.
# AWS_REGION=us-east-1
